# Anticomplementary circumcenter — the circumcenter of the anticomplementary triangle is the orthocenter of ABC (it lies on each altitude) (source: Johnson, Advanced Euclidean Geometry)
A B C = triangle
A2 = parallelogram(B, A, C)
B2 = parallelogram(A, B, C)
C2 = parallelogram(A, C, B)
O2 = circumcenter(A2, B2, C2)
prove perp(A, O2, B, C)
